<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nahash of Ammon</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. c. 1000 BCE</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nahash was a king of Ammon in the late 11th or early 10th century BCE, known from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hebrew-bible">Hebrew Bible</a>. According to the Book of Samuel he besieged <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jabesh-gilead">Jabesh-Gilead</a> and was defeated by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saul">Saul</a>, whose victory confirmed his kingship. His son Hanun later insulted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/david">David</a>'s envoys, provoking a war in which Israel took the Ammonite capital, Rabbah.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nahash-of-ammon.jpg" alt="Nahash of Ammon" width="320" height="435" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AnonymousUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Morgan_Picture_Bible_001.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
